Article 17

(1) Prevention of violence against women is carried out in the following fields:

a. education;
b. health;
c. religion;
d. security;
e. justice;
f. public works and spatial planning;
g. public housing and settlement areas; h. social affairs;
i. manpower;
j. women empowerment and child protection; k. land affairs;
l. environment;
m. population administration and civil registration; n. population control and family planning; o. transportation;
p. communication and informatics;
q. cooperatives, small and medium enterprises;
r. youth and sports;
s. culture;
t. tourism;
u. trade and industry; and
v. other related fields.
(2) Prevention of violence against women as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out in the following forms:
a. developing communication media, information, education and public campaigns through media;
b. developing educational materials and curricula; c. developing safe transportation systems and public spaces;
d. establishing early detection systems, security and integrated complaint services in industrial areas, companies, residential areas, educational environments, Islamic boarding schools and other public spaces;
e. providing consultation services for families, prospective brides and grooms, students, Islamic boarding school students, youth, university students and vulnerable groups;
f. encouraging behavioral change of parents and the community;
g. developing policies related to regencies/cities, villages, schools, Islamic boarding schools, and universities that are safe and friendly for women and integrated with regional spatial planning policies;
h. forming and developing cadres, communities, and groups from among youth, students, Islamic boarding school students, university students, journalists, social media influencers, educators, and religious leaders for prevention;
i. conducting education and advocacy to owners, managers and/or users of social media;
j. developing special protection and support systems for vulnerable groups of women;
k. conducting awareness-raising for perpetrators;
l. conducting cooperation among those responsible for prevention of violence against women; and m. conducting socialization of laws and regulations. (3) The fields and forms of prevention of violence against women as referred to in paragraphs (1) and (2) shall be the responsibility of Regional Apparatus that oversee related affairs.

Article 41

(1) Guidance and supervision as referred to in Article 40 shall be implemented with the following activities: a. regular coordination;

b. preparation of modules and work guidelines;

c. technical guidance and training;

d. preparation of standard operating procedures;

e. providing facilities and mechanisms for managing complaints or grievances related to services for women victims from the community;

f. service access testing;

g. mapping and assessment;

h. resolution of inter-agency disputes;

i. monitoring and evaluation; and

j. reporting.

(2) Guidance and supervision shall be implemented at least 1 (one) time in 1 (one) year.

(3) The results of the implementation of guidance and supervision shall be reported to the Regent.

REGENT OF MAMUJU

REGENT OF MAMUJU

WEST SULAWESI PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF MAMUJU REGENCY

NUMBER 9 YEAR 2023

CONCERNING

EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION OF WOMEN

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF MAMUJU,

Considering : a. that the fulfillment of constitutional rights and protection of women's human rights regarding the empowerment and protection of women is one of the values enshrined in Pancasila and the 1945 Constitution;

b. that women play a very important role in the process of continuation and creation of quality generations so that they require a sense of security, receive guarantees of protection from acts of violence and discrimination and need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally;

c. that based on Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government as mentioned in the Appendix it is stated that the division of government affairs in the field of women's empowerment with one of the sub-affairs being the protection of women;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a, b and c it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Empowerment and Protection of Women;

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 29 Year 1959 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Sulawesi (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1959 Number 74, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia

Number 1822);

3. Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 6 Year 2023 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 Year 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);

4. Law Number 12 Year 2022 concerning the Crime of Sexual Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6792);

With the Joint Approval of

THE REGIONAL PEOPLE'S REPRESENTATIVE COUNCIL OF MAMUJU REGENCY and

THE REGENT OF MAMUJU

DECIDES:

To Enact: REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION OF WOMEN.

