Article 3

(1) Every woman has the right to:

a. live and maintain life and improve her standard of living;
b. fulfill her basic needs to grow and develop properly, have a family and procreate;
c. develop her personality, obtain education, and improve her quality of life to become a person who is faithful, devout, responsible, of noble character, happy, and prosperous in accordance with human rights;
d. obtain justice, security, and freedom to express opinions without discrimination;
e. be involved in every stage of the development process; f. be free from slavery or enslavement
g. be free from threats;
h. obtain protection of her person, family, honor, dignity and property rights;
i. obtain welfare and a decent life; j. participate in politics, economics, social and culture;
k. perform legal acts; and
l. freely choose a spouse in her marriage. (2) Every wife during the marriage bond has the same rights and responsibilities as her husband over all matters concerning her married life, relationship with her children, and ownership and management of joint property in accordance with the applicable laws and regulations. (3) After the dissolution of a marriage, a woman has rights and responsibilities with her former husband over all matters concerning the children with due regard to the best interests of the child.

