a. providing services to women victims of violence in accordance with standard operating procedures; b. conducting coordination of prevention, services and referrals among government-owned service institutions, community-owned service institutions, professional organizations, law enforcement agencies and other related institutions;
c. conducting data collection on case services;
d. providing various information needed by victims, victims' families and the community;
e. conducting prevention of recurrence of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women; f. conducting monitoring and evaluation of victim services; and
g. providing capacity building, guidance and assistance related to victim services.

Article 29

(1) Repatriation and social reintegration services as referred to in Article 24 paragraph (1) letter e shall be implemented with the following activities:

a. repatriation and/or pick-up of victims; b. provision of population documents or personal identity;
c. alternative family;
d. scholarships and educational support facilities; e. non-formal education;
f. skills training and economic enterprises; g. financial assistance and business capital;
h. economic enterprise assistance;
i. housing assistance;
j. food and/or nutrition assistance for victims and their families;
k. provision of social protection programs and poverty alleviation programs;
l. other forms of repatriation and social reintegration services needed by victims.
(2) Repatriation and social reintegration services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be provided to victims, families and persons whose lives depend on victims with the aim that victims have the readiness and ability to live in society.
(3) Repatriation and social reintegration services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out in an integrated manner with the Integrated Referral Service System for social protection and poverty alleviation and the Child Social Welfare Center.
(4) Repatriation and social reintegration services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be the responsibility of the Regional Apparatus managing:
a. social affairs;
b. population administration and civil registration affairs;
c. labor affairs;
d. cooperative, small and medium enterprise affairs; e. education affairs;
f. health affairs;
g. public works and spatial planning affairs; h. land affairs, women's empowerment and child protection affairs; and
i. other related affairs.
